We tried to fix some world generation bugs, which affected the save system. In this regard, we will be forced to reset the saved data of game locations. Compensation for the inconvenience is planned for all players. We apologize for this.

[b]How to start the game with the previous character:[/b]
To continue the game with your hero, start a new game first without prologue (tutorial), and after the first cutscene and dialog leaving the wagon will go to the main menu, and then the option “Load” will be available. Choose your past character and continue the game with him.

[b]About the translation of the game into Brazilian and Spanish: [/b]
We have not forgotten, and we are still working on the translation.

[b]LIST OF PATCH CHANGES:[/b]
- Fixed a critical error with the change of weapons;
- Improved design of the action bar;
- Identified and eliminated some causes of memory leaks;
- Improved interface;
- Added crafting help;
- Added image quality customization;
- Added rewards for daily login;
- New item - Homemade sickle;
- New item - Simple Survival Guide;
- New item - Survival Manual;
- New item - Advanced Survival Guide;
- Changed some crafting items;
- Changed the structure of the main menu;
- Performed some minor optimization work on the project;
- Added Control Guide in Game Settings for Keyboard (you can't reassign buttons yet).

Please check if all the bugs you found earlier are up to date.
If you find new critical bugs, please inform us in the Discord server of the game: https://discord.gg/fRJ26z9Q8b

[b]Patch 0.2.2[/b] - Small changes and fixes based on your feedback!

We thank everyone for their trust and feedback. We are doing our best to fix critical bugs, as well as introduce improvements to the game based on your feedback whenever possible.

For better and faster support, we have launched an official [url=https://discord.gg/fRJ26z9Q8b]Discord[/url] game server.

[b]List of Patch Changes:[/b].
- Found and fixed some critical bugs;
- Found and fixed several causes of memory leaks;
- Improved the system of interaction with items;
- Increased inventory volume;
- Added a lighter to the starting inventory;
- Added character vigor indicator;
- New item - Lens;
- New item - Sleeping Pill. (Decreases vigor so you can go to bed immediately);
- New item - Coffee (Increases Vigor);
- Changed the purpose of energy bars and energy bars;
- Fixed several inventory related bugs;
- Added a slot to the inventory for quick removal of items;
- Added the ability to start a new game.

[b]Patch 0.2.1a[/b] - Fixes critical bugs based on your feedback!

[b]Patch change list:[/b]
- Fixed a critical bug with the fishing rod;
- Found and fixed several causes of memory leaks;
- Fixed the disappearance of items in crates after a game crash;
- Improved the algorithm of saving-loading the world;
- New hints were introduced in the prologue;
- Fixed errors with moving objects (objects could disappear under certain conditions);
- Fixed a critical bug in the biome "Cemetery";
- Fixed a pause bug (Time progression continued while the game was paused);
- Changed some crafts.

[b]Patch 0.2.1[/b] - Small changes and fixes based on your feedback!

[b]Patch Changes List:[/b]
- Fixed bugs in the prologue quest stages;
- Fixed some localization bugs;
- Inventory and other interface elements will now close during stun;
- Finalized prologue completion condition;
- Added a notification when trying to open a pause in the prologue;
- Found and fixed several causes of memory leaks;
- New item - Subcorner (can be obtained from young trees, needed to create rope);
- Added a new rope craft;
- Added equipment comparison feature;
- Bonfire no longer sets your character on fire;
- Fixed a bug when entering your character's name when starting a new game.

The day has come when we can announce the [b]Early Access[/b] release of iZolated from developer Crooked Road on August 12, 2024 on Steam!

[b]- Why Early Access.[/b]
"We desperately need feedback and communication from the community, taking the ideas and feedback from the community we want to improve our game and release a bug-free version."

[b]- How long will the game be in early access?[/b]
"We estimate that the game will be in early access for 8 to 12 months."

[b]- How will the full version differ from the early access version?[/b]
"We plan to add the following:
- Steam achievements;
- New story chapters;
- More quests;
- More recipes for Crafting;
- Improve gamepad support;
- New enemies;
- Community recommendations will be taken into account;
- New locations, weapons, dungeons."

[b]- What will be the status of the Early Access version?[/b]
"Early Access" introduces the first chapter of the game and contains an extensive area with quests, various enemies, as well as the first 16 achievements for Steam and VK Play.
Right now you can play for 8-14 hours. By release, we expect it to be 25-60 hours."

[b]- Will the price of the game be different during and after Early Access?[/b]
"There is a possibility that the price at release will be higher than in Early Access."

[b]- How do you plan to involve the community in the development process?[/b]
"We plan to develop our game interactively with the community on platforms such as Discord and Steam, where you can express your ideas and participate in polls."

[b]List of innovations of patch 0.2.0:[/b]
- Finalized the design of locations;
- Redesigned mechanics of interaction with objects;
- Added 15 quests of the quest board;
- Added 16 first achievements;
- Finalized prologue;
- New "Summer Lake" structure;
- New biome "Beach";
- New biome "Red Zone";
- Slightly changed dialogs with NPCs;
- Changed some sprites;
- Now on the beds you can grow all kinds of mushrooms (including fluorescent), plantain, alfalfa, chamomile;
- Opened access to caves;
- Improved construction mechanics;
- New mutant: Ogre;
- Introduced mutants: Siren, Fogger, Shrub Mimic;
- New Infected types: Paramedic, Medic, Firefighter;
- New item - Construction Hammer;
- New item - Log Wall;
- New item - Log Fence;
- New item - Brick Wall;
- New item - Painkiller;
- New item - Small bed (for planting small plants);
- New item - Small trap (device for hunting small animals);
- New item - Feather;
- New item - Bird feeder;
- New item - Trophy Rack (Also added trophy heads of each mutant species);
- New item - Radio (story item for communicating with others);
- New item - Red Dye;
- New item - Green Dye;
- New item - Blue Dye;
- New item - Blueberry (can be eaten);
- Swimsuits (3 colors for each gender of the character) have been added along with the beach.

Please note that the introduction of Achievements in the game required the need to update the game engine, which led to changes in the syntax of the game code. Critical errors and partial or incorrect operation of Achievements are possible.

[b]Please report any bugs you find in the discussions![/b]

[b]We continue to work on improving the game before the game release![/b]

The following changes have been made to the demo version of the game:
- Added a new zone - Gas station;
- Added new items and crafting blueprints;
- Improved artificial intelligence of enemies;
- Added two small quests;
- Updated object sprites;
- Expanded zone boundaries;
- Added food rotting in inventory (now food and other products have an expiration date, this mechanic will be useful for crafting new items).

All bugs and errors found can be reported directly to tech support at lt_games_group@vk.com


[b]We are also pleased to officially announce that early access to the game will be available on August 1, 2024![/b] This will help us to continue working on the development of the game, and all players will be able to receive story updates for free, and the price of the game will not change after the release of the game.
